H1600.definition:
a primitive root;
to bellow (as cattle)
KJV: low.

H1601.definition:
feminine active participle of H1600 (גָּעָה); lowing;
Goah, a place near Jerusalem
KJV: Goath.

H1602.definition:
a primitive root;
to detest; by implication, to reject
KJV: abhor, fail, lothe, vilely cast away.

H1603.definition:
from H1602 (גָּעַל); loathing;
Gaal, an Israelite
KJV: Gaal.

H1605.definition:
a primitive root;
to chide
KJV: corrupt, rebuke, reprove.

H1606.definition:
from H1605 (גָּעַר);
a chiding
KJV: rebuke(-ing), reproof.

H1608.definition:
from H1607 (גָּעַשׁ); a quaking;
Gaash, a hill in Palestine
KJV: Gaash.

H1609.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Gatam, an Edomite
KJV: Gatam.

H1610.definition:
from an unused root meaning to arch;
the back; by extension the body or self
KJV: [phrase] highest places, himself.

H1611.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1610 (גַּף);
a wing
KJV: wing.

H1612.definition:
from an unused root meaning to bend;
a vine (as twining), especially the grape
KJV: vine, tree.

H1613.definition:
from an unused root, probably meaning to house in;
a kind of tree or wood (as used for building), apparently the cypress
KJV: gopher.

H1614.definition:
probably feminine of H1613 (גֹּפֶר);
properly, cypress-resin; by analogy, sulphur (as equally inflammable)
KJV: brimstone.

H1615.definition:
perhaps from H3564 (כּוּר);
lime (from being burned in a kiln)
KJV: chalk(-stone).

H1616.definition:
or (fully) geyr (gare); from H1481 (גּוּר);
properly, a guest; by implication, a foreigner
KJV: alien, sojourner, stranger.

H1617.definition:
perhaps from H1626 (גֵּרָה); a grain;
Gera, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Gera.

H1618.definition:
from an unused root meaning to scratch;
scurf (from itching)
KJV: scab, scurvy.

H1619.definition:
from the same as H1618 (גָּרָב); scabby;
Gareb, the name of an Israelite, also of a hill near Jerusalem
KJV: Gareb.

H1620.definition:
by reduplication from H1641 (גָּרַר);
a berry (as if a pellet of rumination)
KJV: berry.

H1621.definition:
feminine plural from H1641 (גָּרַר);
the throat (as used in rumination)
KJV: neck.

H1622.definition:
patrial from an unused name (of uncertain derivation);
a Girgashite, one of the native tribes of Canaan
KJV: Girgashite, Girgasite.

H1623.definition:
a primitive root;
to abrade
KJV: scrape.

H1624.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to grate, i.e. (figuratively) to anger
KJV: contend, meddle, stir up, strive.

H1625.definition:
from H1641 (גָּרַר);
the cud (as scraping the throat)
KJV: cud.

H1628.definition:
from H1481 (גּוּר);
a (temporary) residence
KJV: habitation.

H1629.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut off
KJV: cut off.

H1630.definition:
plural of an unused noun from H1629 (גָּרַז) (compare H1511 (גִּזְרִי)), cut up (i.e. rocky);
Gerizim, a mountain of Palestine
KJV: Gerizim.

H1631.definition:
from H1629 (גָּרַז);
an axe
KJV: ax.

H1632.definition:
from the same as H1486 (גּוֹרָל);
harsh
KJV: man of great (as in the margin which reads H1419 (גָּדוֹל)).

H1633.definition:
a primitive root; to be spare or skeleton-like; used only as a denominative from H1634 (גֶּרֶם);
(causative) to bone, i.e. denude (by extensive, craunch) the bones
KJV: gnaw the bones, break.

H1634.definition:
from H1633 (גָּרַם);
a bone (as the skeleton of the body); hence, self, i.e. (figuratively) very
KJV: bone, strong, top.

H1635.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1634 (גֶּרֶם);
a bone
KJV: bone.

H1636.definition:
from H1634 (גֶּרֶם);
bony, i.e. strong
KJV: Garmite.

H1637.definition:
from an unused root meaning to smooth;
a threshing-floor (as made even); by analogy, any open area
KJV: (barn, corn, threshing-) floor, (threshing-, void) place.

H1638.definition:
a primitive root;
to crush; also (intransitively and figuratively) to dissolve
KJV: break.

H1639.definition:
a primitive root;
to scrape off; by implication, to shave, remove, lessen, withhold
KJV: abate, clip, (di-) minish, do (take) away, keep back, restrain, make small, withdraw.

H1640.definition:
a primitive root;
to bear off violently
KJV: sweep away.

H1641.definition:
a primitive root;
to drag off roughly; by implication, to bring up the cud (i.e. ruminate); by analogy, to saw
KJV: catch, chew, [idiom] continuing, destroy, saw.

H1642.definition:
probably from H1641 (גָּרַר); a rolling country;
Gerar, a Philistine city
KJV: Gerar.

H1643.definition:
from an unused root meaning to husk;
a kernel (collectively), i.e. grain
KJV: beaten corn.

H1644.definition:
a primitive root;
to drive out from a possession; especially to expatriate or divorce
KJV: cast up (out), divorced (woman), drive away (forth, out), expel, [idiom] surely put away, trouble, thrust out.

H1645.definition:
from H1644 (גָּרַשׁ);
produce (as if expelled)
KJV: put forth.

H1646.definition:
feminine passive participle of H1644 (גָּרַשׁ);
(abstractly) dispossession
KJV: exaction.

H1647.definition:
for H1648 (גֵּרְשׁוֹן);
Gereshom, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Gershom.

H1648.definition:
or גֵּרְשׁוֹם; from H1644 (גָּרַשׁ); a refugee;
Gereshon or Gereshom, an Israelite
KJV: Gershon, Gershom.

H1649.definition:
patronymically from H1648 (גֵּרְשׁוֹן);
a Gereshonite or descendant of Gereshon
KJV: Gershonite, sons of Gershon.

H1650.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to join); bridge;
Geshur, a district of Syria
KJV: Geshur, Geshurite.

H1651.definition:
patrial from H1650 (גְּשׁוּר);
a Geshurite (also collectively) or inhabitants of Geshur
KJV: Geshuri, Geshurites.

H1652.definition:
a primitive root;
to shower violently
KJV: (cause to) rain.

H1653.definition:
from H1652 (גָּשַׁם);
a shower
KJV: rain, shower.

H1654.definition:
or (prolonged) גַּשְׁמוּ; the same as H1653 (גֶּשֶׁם);
Geshem or Gashmu, an Arabian
KJV: Geshem, Gashmu.

H1655.definition:
(Aramaic) apparently the same as H1653 (גֶּשֶׁם);
used in a peculiar sense, the body (probably for the (figuratively) idea of a hard rain)
KJV: body.

H1656.definition:
from H1652 (גָּשַׁם); equivalent to H1653 (גֶּשֶׁם)
{a shower}
KJV: rained upon.

H1657.definition:
probably of Egyptian origin;
Goshen, the residence of the Israelites in Egypt; also a place in Palestine
KJV: Goshen.

H1658.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Gishpa, an Israelite
KJV: Gispa.

H1660.definition:
probably from H5059 (נָגַן) (in the sense of treading out grapes);
a wine-press (or vat for holding the grapes in pressing them)
KJV: (wine-) press (fat).

H1661.definition:
the same as H1660 (גַּת);
Gath, a Philistine city
KJV: Gath.

H1662.definition:
or (abridged) גִּתָּה־חֵפֶר; from H1660 (גַּת) and H2658 (חָפַר) with the article inserted; wine-press of (the) well;
Gath-Chepher, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gath-kephr, Gittah-kephr.

H1663.definition:
patrial from H1661 (גַּת);
a Gittite or inhabitant of Gath
KJV: Gittite.

H1664.definition:
dual of H1660 (גַּת); double winepress;
Gittajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gittaim.

H1665.definition:
feminine of H1663 (גִּתִּי);
a Gittite harp
KJV: Gittith.

H1666.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Gether, a son of Aram, and the region settled by him
KJV: Gether.

H1667.definition:
from H1660 (גַּת) and H7416 (רִמּוֹן); wine-press of (the) pomegranate;
Gath-Rimmon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gath-rimmon. d

H1668.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2088 (זֶה);
this
KJV: one..another, this.

H1669.definition:
a primitive root;
to pine
KJV: mourn, sorrow(-ful).

H1670.definition:
from H1669 (דָּאַב);
properly, pining; by analogy, fear
KJV: sorrow.

H1672.definition:
a primitive root;
be anxious
KJV: be afraid (careful, sorry), sorrow, take thought.

H1673.definition:
or (fully) דּוֹאֵג; active participle of H1672 (דָּאַג); anxious;
Doeg, an Edomite
KJV: Doeg.

H1674.definition:
from H1672 (דָּאַג);
anxiety
KJV: care(-fulness), fear, heaviness, sorrow.

H1675.definition:
a primitive root;
to dart, i.e. fly rapidly
KJV: fly.

H1676.definition:
from H1675 (דָּאָה);
the kite (from its rapid flight)
KJV: vulture. See H7201 (רָאָה).

H1677.definition:
or (fully) דּוֹב; from H1680 (דָּבַב);
the bear (as slow)
KJV: bear.

H1678.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1677 (דֹּב)
{the bear (as slow)}
KJV: bear.

H1679.definition:
from an unused root (compare H1680 (דָּבַב)) (probably meaning to be sluggish, i.e. restful);
quiet
KJV: strength.

H1680.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1679 (דֹּבֶא));
to move slowly, i.e. glide
KJV: cause to speak.

H1681.definition:
from H1680 (דָּבַב) (in the sense of furtive motion);
slander
KJV: defaming, evil report, infamy, slander.

H1682.definition:
or (shortened) דְּבֹרָה; from H1696 (דָבַר) (in the sense of orderly motion);
the bee (from its systematic instincts)
KJV: bee.

H1683.definition:
or (shortened) דְּבֹרָה; the same as H1682 (דְּבוֹרָה);
Deborah, the name of two Hebrewesses
KJV: Deborah.

H1684.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2076 (זָבַח);
to sacrifice (an animal)
KJV: offer (sacrifice).

H1685.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1684 (דְּבַח);
a sacrifice
KJV: sacrifice.

H1687.definition:
or (shortened) דְּבִר; from H1696 (דָבַר) (apparently in the sense of oracle);
the shrine or innermost part of the sanctuary
KJV: oracle.

H1688.definition:
or (shortened) דְּבִר; (Joshua 13:26 (but see H3810 (לֹא דְבַר))), the same as H1687 (דְּבִיר);
Debir, the name of an Amoritish king and of two places in Palestine
KJV: Debir.

H1689.definition:
probably an orthographical error for H7247 (רִבְלָה);
Diblah, a place in Syria
KJV: Diblath.

H1690.definition:
from an unused root (akin to H2082 (זָבַל)) probably meaning to press together;
a cake of pressed figs
KJV: cake (lump) of figs.

H1691.definition:
dual from the masculine of H1690 (דְּבֵלָה); two cakes;
Diblajim, a symbolic name
KJV: Diblaim.

H1692.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to impinge, i.e. cling or adhere; figuratively, to catch by pursuit
KJV: abide fast, cleave (fast together), follow close (hard after), be joined (together), keep (fast), overtake, pursue hard, stick, take.

H1693.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1692 (דָּבַק);
to stick to
KJV: cleave.

H1694.definition:
from H1692 (דָּבַק);
a joint; by implication, solder
KJV: joint, solder.

H1695.definition:
from H1692 (דָּבַק);
adhering
KJV: cleave, joining, stick closer.

H1696.definition:
a primitive root;
perhaps properly, to arrange; but used figuratively (of words), to speak; rarely (in a destructive sense) to subdue
KJV: answer, appoint, bid, command, commune, declare, destroy, give, name, promise, pronounce, rehearse, say, speak, be spokesman, subdue, talk, teach, tell, think, use (entreaties), utter, [idiom] well, [idiom] work.

H1697.definition:
from H1696 (דָבַר);
a word; by implication, a matter (as spoken of) or thing; adverbially, a cause
KJV: act, advice, affair, answer, [idiom] any such (thing), because of, book, business, care, case, cause, certain rate, [phrase] chronicles, commandment, [idiom] commune(-ication), [phrase] concern(-ing), [phrase] confer, counsel, [phrase] dearth, decree, deed, [idiom] disease, due, duty, effect, [phrase] eloquent, errand, (evil favoured-) ness, [phrase] glory, [phrase] harm, hurt, [phrase] iniquity, [phrase] judgment, language, [phrase] lying, manner, matter, message, (no) thing, oracle, [idiom] ought, [idiom] parts, [phrase] pertaining, [phrase] please, portion, [phrase] power, promise, provision, purpose, question, rate, reason, report, request, [idiom] (as hast) said, sake, saying, sentence, [phrase] sign, [phrase] so, some (uncleanness), somewhat to say, [phrase] song, speech, [idiom] spoken, talk, task, [phrase] that, [idiom] there done, thing (concerning), thought, [phrase] thus, tidings, what(-soever), [phrase] wherewith, which, word, work.

H1698.definition:
from H1696 (דָבַר) (in the sense of destroying);
a pestilence
KJV: murrain, pestilence, plague.

H1699.definition:
from H1696 (דָבַר) (in its original sense);
a pasture (from its arrangement of the flock)
KJV: fold, manner.
